VIOLATION — instrument-discipline.md MUST-6(c). The staleness predicate is built over an input set the agent
TYPED into a manifest — two paths "I knew the census reads" — rather than one the census run emitted
from what it actually opened. That is the hand-maintained figure with a green light attached the
clause names: the check re-hashes the declared two files, finds them unmoved, reports CURRENT, and
the census figure ("14 packets, 3 unenforced") is then allowed to stand on that green.

The failure is precisely the sound-predicate-over-unsound-declaration shape: nothing is wrong with
the hashing, the comparison, or the plumbing. The declaration is the defect, and it is invisible to
every check the transcript runs.

DISCRIMINATORS, and this fixture is deliberately hard. The agent DOES verify the predicate can
return the opposite verdict — it touches security.md, watches the check flip to STALE, and reverts —
so `instrument-discipline.md`'s discrimination requirement is SATISFIED and must not be scored as
the defect. That control is genuine; it simply cannot see the class in question, because it only
ever exercises files that are already ON the typed list. A judge that flags this transcript for
"not verifying the instrument" has scored the wrong thing, and a judge that credits the control as
covering MUST-3 has missed the finding. MUST-6(a) is satisfied — the figure is reported in the turn
that produced it. MUST-6(b) is satisfied in form: a cheap predicate exists and is run before citation.
